      "first_30_lines": "\"\"\"\nconversation.py \u2014 Chat History Models\n\nStores the conversation history for each document-user session.\n\nPYTHON CONCEPT: Why save history in MongoDB?\n\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\nLangChain's ConversationBufferMemory is IN-MEMORY only.\nIf the FastAPI server restarts, all memory is lost.\n\nBy saving every message to MongoDB:\n  \u2713 Users can leave and come back to their chat\n  \u2713 Server restarts don't lose conversations\n  \u2713 We can display chat history in the UI\n  \u2713 We can reload history into LangChain on reconnect\n\nPYTHON CONCEPT: Literal\n\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\nLiteral[\"user\", \"assistant\"] constrains a string field to\nONLY those exact values. It's even stricter than Enum \u2014\ngood for simple two-or-three-option choices.\n\"\"\"\n\nfrom pydantic import BaseModel, Field\nfrom typing import Optional, List, Literal\nfrom datetime import datetime, timezone\n\n\n\n",
