      "first_30_lines": "\"\"\"\ndatabase.py \u2014 MongoDB Connection Manager\n\nPYTHON CONCEPT: Module-Level State\n\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\nIn Python, when you import a module, it runs ONCE\nand the results are cached. So this file creates\nthe database client exactly once \u2014 every file that\nimports `db` gets the same connection object.\n\nThis is equivalent to:\n    // db.js in Node.js\n    const mongoose = require('mongoose')\n    mongoose.connect(MONGODB_URI)\n    module.exports = mongoose.connection\n\nPYTHON CONCEPT: Motor (Async MongoDB)\n\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\nMotor is the async MongoDB driver for Python.\n- Mongoose (Node) \u2192 Motor (Python)\n- Both wrap the same MongoDB operations\n- Motor uses Python's async/await instead of JS Promises\n\nKey difference from Mongoose:\n  Mongoose has schemas built-in.\n  Motor is schema-less (like the raw MongoDB driver in Node).\n  We define schemas separately using Pydantic models.\n\"\"\"\n\nimport motor.motor_asyncio",
